-- examples/checks/agg-join-delta-first.rofl — A JOIN THAT ONLY A DELTA-FIRST PLAN FITS IN THE SPACE.
--
-- hit(Y, Z) :- h(X, Z), l(X, Y), trig(Y, Z). h and l are 100 rows each, all with X = c, so
-- h joined to l is 10000 rows, which is more than the space of its check (250), while trig is
-- three rows and binds Y and Z. In written order the firing on the news of h (or of l) joins
-- h to l first and holds all 10000 rows. The delta-first plan (engine/joinplan.rs) starts from
-- the news and takes the premise with the fewest matches next, trig, and holds a handful. In
-- the engine's written order this world is a space wall; with the plan it is not
-- (agg_breaks `delta_first_off`).
edb(h). edb(l). edb(trig).
hit(Y, Z) :- h(X, Z), l(X, Y), trig(Y, Z).
